                            "очень большой по количеству; неисчислимый, бесчисленный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d4d9a36a-ff2a-4d0f-af71-f8166075b6f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "0a8e2cb6-28b8-3064-a0f3-cb5e21c3c9a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "5710e11b-b169-33bc-bf0e-103698d41b77",
                        "target_lang_word": "innumerable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "innumerable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c502f446-bf1e-3d59-8df8-c40dc8828aed",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1c6af6-6996-33a5-a0e8-63368ce3390c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not capable of being counted, enumerated, or numbered."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42f6d90c-74dc-409f-afcf-d44fc962557d",
                                                "sense_id": "c502f446-bf1e-3d59-8df8-c40dc8828aed",
                                                "text": "The casualties of the Second World War were so great that they are innumerable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "561b9d6a-de35-4fc8-a0e1-18f59d3c98d2",
                                                "sense_id": "c502f446-bf1e-3d59-8df8-c40dc8828aed",
                                                "text": "Soon we could see the innumerable banners fluttering, and then the sun struck the sea of armor and set it all aflash."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fb2f2aa-14e1-3fed-8b62-d35966ef7e54",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1c6af6-6996-33a5-a0e8-63368ce3390c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a very high number; extremely numerous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c75611c-50af-4c75-a71b-27eb38a140fa",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb2f2aa-14e1-3fed-8b62-d35966ef7e54",
                                                "text": "Kjelsås (six miles) marks the end of the suburbs, and the line immediately plunges into Nordmarka. This vast untamed area of forest and mountain (much of it over 2,000 ft. above sea level), interspersed with innumerable lakes, large and small, is known as Oslo's playground."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5bee525-905c-4c23-9899-c4bc61d52640",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb2f2aa-14e1-3fed-8b62-d35966ef7e54",
                                                "text": "The wide sandy plain of the valley, some five miles long, which slopes imperceptibly down to Issik Pakhta, is overgrown with minute bushes. All the tiny streams we crossed unite to form the Alessun Gol, which then flows westwards to the pasture grounds of Kala Otlak. We observed dozens of herds of orongo, mainly females, with innumerable young. The landscape looked highly unpromising for agriculture yet I noticed that the folk of Bulaq Bashi planted grain. Four hours’ marching took us to within sight of Issik Pakhta Nor, which the maps also record as Khon Qum Nor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1dae39d-ffca-4258-82d9-af0fb83a3a30",
                        "source_entry_id": "0a8e2cb6-28b8-3064-a0f3-cb5e21c3c9a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "5710e11b-b169-33bc-bf0e-103698d41b77",
                        "target_lang_word": "countless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "countless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8dd35012-a627-359c-a6e5-f9b9f4ea2de0",
                                        "entry_id": "623b9d2f-da8a-34ed-9769-43d84289d5a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A huge and uncountable number of; too many to count; innumerable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a count noun"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46d679d9-ba87-46fd-8344-1bf6ee71a2eb",
                                                "sense_id": "8dd35012-a627-359c-a6e5-f9b9f4ea2de0",
                                                "text": "There are countless stars in the sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9553a05-572c-44c9-b646-a52bdbe72fd8",
                                                "sense_id": "8dd35012-a627-359c-a6e5-f9b9f4ea2de0",
                                                "text": "He endured countless insults hurled at him before people finally respected him for his courage and his great ability as a baseball player."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "countless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de59ba78-9dc6-3872-9c5c-bf729ab76891",
                                        "entry_id": "c4e4d6ee-299b-359a-8fc5-0427793a8353",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of uncountable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "589616e1-991a-499f-8ee3-2cf1143794cc",
                                                "sense_id": "de59ba78-9dc6-3872-9c5c-bf729ab76891",
                                                "text": "The stars in the sky are countless."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a0d6863-0886-3cec-b52c-57633ed17dae",
                                        "entry_id": "c4e4d6ee-299b-359a-8fc5-0427793a8353",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Too large to be counted to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bfe3c88-a4ad-4159-a443-6ad51f1b114c",
                                                "sense_id": "0a0d6863-0886-3cec-b52c-57633ed17dae",
                                                "text": "Just stop and think deeply for a moment and realize the countless number of the grains of sand of the seashore; the countless number of drops of water that go to make up the waters of the earth; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
